    "result_text": "All 17 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for owners. The flow: `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 service \u2192 the code is serialized back via `OwnerDto` on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java` model** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to a new `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 before persisting, calls a new `generateCustomerCode(lastName)` helper that builds `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (falls back to the whole name if shorter than 3).\n   - `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits via `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`.\n   - Computed before `saveOwner`, so the count reflects owners existing at creation time and increments by one per create (the global sequence property the test asserts).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema so it's part of the generated `OwnerDto` and returned in responses (MapStruct auto-maps it by name).\n\n4. **Schema files** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `customer_code` column. Tests run on the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist in `schema.sql`.\n\nThe `Cp09Tests.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` test verifies `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the two sequential creates differ by exactly 1 \u2014 both now pass, along with the full suite.",
